,"gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-24T19:43:33Z","updated_at":"2025-04-24T19:44:29Z","body":"> Alternatively you can keep invert() in LocalVector and make it call reverse() (and wrap in DISABLE_DEPRECATED checks).\r\n\r\nI plan to do that in godot-cpp. I don't think it's needed for Godot internal.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2828686443/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2828772826","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101027#issuecomment-2828772826","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101027","id":2828772826,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6om6Xa","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-24T20:24:59Z","updated_at":"2025-04-24T20:24:59Z","body":"> > Alternatively you can keep invert() in LocalVector and make it call reverse() (and wrap in DISABLE_DEPRECATED checks).\r\n> \r\n> I plan to do that in godot-cpp. I don't think it's needed for Godot internal.\r\n\r\nThe point is that it's technically compat breaking for C++ modules external to this repository too, or forks/thirdparty platforms, etc.\r\n\r\nKeeping the deprecated version as an alias helps those users transition to 4.5, and possibly keep their modules compatible with multiple Godot versions without having to include `core/version.h` just to check which API to use.\r\n\r\nThat being said, with all the files reorganization we're doing in 4.5, it's pretty much going to require exactly this kind of `GODOT_VERSION` checks to maintain modules that support both 4.4 and 4.5, so adding this one wouldn't hurt much.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2828772826/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2828801437","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101027#issuecomment-2828801437","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101027","id":2828801437,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6onBWd","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gr